  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Order of words in time",
   "texto": [
    "If a time expression goes to the beginning, the conjugated verb takes second place: Om morgenen står jeg opp («In the morning I get up»). The Spanish usually keep the order subtent- verb.",
    "In a main sentence, ofte («a menudo»), altid («always») and aldri («never») usually go after the conjugated verb: Jeg jobber ofte.",
    "After må («have to») goes the infinitive without å: Jeg må jobbe («I have to work.»), it is not added å in front of the infinitive."
   ]
  },
